Nethack is about not dying long enough to win for you, and you haven't
done it yet. :) For some of us (and maybe this number is small), it's
actually about something different, item identification and clever
usage; Derek's change here takes the approach of damaging the player by
attrition rather than outright killing her. This is a little more Crawly
than most NetHack effects, but I don't think that's necessarily bad;
plenty of people die at Crawl. 

In general, Nethack could stand to burn up player resources more between
the Castle and the Planes; making Max HP something that can go _down_ if
you're not paying attention or burning resources on high-level casters is
certainly one way to do that.

> Compare and contrast "oh, whine, an instance where
> patience play gives some players an unfair advantage
> over those of us too impatient to employ such
> methods; this must not be allowed to endure".

Leaving this largely aside, it's worth pointing out that draining maxHP
will even cut into uber-pumped characters a little bit; 900HP behemoths
can't necessarily just ignore three purple Ls anymore. I think I like 
this change, though I'm reserving a final opinion for playtesting.

